# Alembic migrations for Spotlight

Real database migrations for the persistent store (Postgres in
production, SQLite in dev / tests). Replaces the pre-P1.4 best-effort
`Base.metadata.create_all` on API startup.

## Where things live

- `alembic.ini`            — top-level Alembic config; the sqlalchemy.url
                              is overridden at runtime by env.py when
                              `DATABASE_URL` is set.
- `alembic/env.py`          — loads `spotlight.store.models.Base.metadata`
                              as the autogenerate target and normalises
                              the `postgres://` → `postgresql+psycopg://`
                              scheme SQLAlchemy 2.0 requires.
- `alembic/versions/`       — every migration script. Files are prefixed
                              with a random 12-char id and a short slug.

## Runbook

Apply the current schema to a fresh database:

```
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://user:pass@host/db alembic upgrade head
```

Autogenerate a new migration after editing models:

```
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "short slug describing the change"
# review the generated file — the Text() import in JSONB.astext_type is
# frequently omitted, add `from sqlalchemy import Text` if so
alembic upgrade head        # apply locally
```

Roll back one revision (dev / testing only):

```
alembic downgrade -1
```

## Deploy hook

`infra/Dockerfile.api` runs `alembic upgrade head` before starting the
API process. The command is idempotent — re-running with no pending
migrations is a no-op — so it is safe on every container start.

When we split the API and worker into separate services (P1.2), the
worker's Dockerfile uses the same entrypoint pattern. Both replicas will
attempt the upgrade; Alembic uses a table-level advisory lock (Postgres)
so only the first one actually applies changes.

## Development / test convenience

`spotlight.store.init_schema()` continues to call
`Base.metadata.create_all` for unit tests and CLI runners that use an
in-memory SQLite database — running `alembic upgrade head` per test
would be wasteful. Production paths never touch `init_schema` — they
rely on `alembic upgrade head` in the container entrypoint.

## Baseline revision

`ef7e82e2bcc5_baseline_schema.py` captures the entire schema at
paper-v1 / Week 3 durability landing:

- sweeps, findings, events, sweep_jobs, pr_watches, workspace_prefs,
  findings_filter_prefs
- sweep_jobs.heartbeat_at (P1.1 — multi-worker lease heartbeat)
- events UNIQUE(sweep_id, seq) as uq_events_sweep_seq (P1.3 — idempotent
  event insert under crash-retry)

All future migrations chain off this baseline.
